Exceptions Practice

Exceptions are unexpected incidents that hault execution
Ex: dividing by 0

-----------------------------------------------------------
Try and catch blocks

Try block
	surrounds the normal code
	exits if an exception is thrown within the try block

Catch block
	"extra" code after the try block
	"catches" the thrown try block exception
	if the thrown exception type matches the catch block's parameter type, the code in the catch block executes
	
	also called an execption handler

---------------------------------------------------------------

example with a try and catch block
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.InputMismatchException;

public class LightTravelTime {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
     Scanner scnr = new Scanner(System.in);
     double distMiles = 0.0;
     double lightTravelTimeSec = 0.0;
  
     System.out.print("Enter distance in miles: ");

     try {
        distMiles = scnr.nextDouble();
        lightTravelTimeSec = distMiles / 186282.0;
     }
     catch (InputMismatchException e) {
        System.out.println("Must enter a number!");
     }

     System.out.println(lightTravelTimeSec);
  }
}

Example:
	Enter distance in miles: twenty
	Must enter a number!

